 # bench-sleep-tool (benchmark fixture)
 
-A tiny tool plugin exposing one `sleep` tool, written in the 0.1.1-era style
-(bare `cordis` cohort). The host is moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+A tiny tool plugin exposing one `sleep` tool with cancellation support, on the
+dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cohort. Its declared peers are the packages the registration
+uses: `@deepseek-ai/cordis` (Context) and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` (defineTool,
+ToolRunContext). Tool results are typed as `ContentBlock` from
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm`, a type-only reference the host closure already carries
+as a peer of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` (declaring it as a second 0.1.2-alpha.2
+peer is unresolvable under npm: `dsh-tools`' own `^0.1.2-alpha.2` peer ranges
+resolve to the later `0.1.2-rc.1` prereleases).
+
+The plugin ships no source patch against the harness: its complete surface is
+this package plus the `cordis.patch.yml` bundle layer declared by
+`dsh.bundle.patch`, the profile-composition layer a `dsh plugin add` installs.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
